{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS6Xetub9hTRBUvKLexJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A `save_fact` call should no longer evict the cached system prompt: the next call now writes only the new fact (about 15 tokens) instead of rewriting about 1,000. I checked this with an offline simulation, not against the live API.\n\n**The cause:** the instructions and the athlete's details were sent as one block with one cache marker. The cache matches whole blocks, so adding a fact changed that block, nothing before it counted as already cached, and the next call paid for the whole prompt again. The facts were also in the middle of that text, with `Language:` after them.\n\n**The fix (`build_system` in `bot.py`):** the system prompt is now a list of blocks that only grows at the end:\n1. the static instructions;\n2. the athlete profile: date, name, sport, zones, goal, language and the facts heading;\n3. one block per fact, at the end, in the order they were saved.\n\nThe cache marker goes on the last block. When a fact is added, everything before it is unchanged. The API checks earlier block boundaries (up to about 20 blocks back), so it finds what the previous call cached and writes only the new fact. I also removed the \"(none yet)\" placeholder: replacing it with the first fact would have broken the match.\n\nI didn't just add a second cache marker after the instructions. From the logs, the tools plus instructions come to roughly 950 tokens, below Sonnet 4.5's 1,024-token minimum for caching, so that marker would have done nothing without any error.\n\n**Testing:** I had no API key and made no external calls. I wrote a fake model, kept outside the repo, that caches by matching whole blocks the same way. I ran it through `reply()` for one athlete: a normal message, a fact save, a normal message, another fact save. After the first message, every call found the existing prefix. The round after each fact save wrote one block, and the next message wrote nothing. To confirm on real traffic, look at the round after a `save_fact` in `logs/usage.jsonl`: `cache_read_input_tokens` should be about the previous total, and `cache_creation_input_tokens` about 15–20.\n\n**Not changed:** messages that switch on the planning or race tools still miss the cache, because tools come before the system prompt. Those are the 1,305- and 1,334-token writes in the log. The next normal message still uses the cache. This comes from the keyword-based tool filtering, which `NOTES.md` says to keep, so I left it.\n\nTo keep caching working, facts must stay at the end in the order they were saved, and nothing that changes per message should go into the system blocks. `ANSWER.md` has the full write-up, and I updated the caching sentence in `README.md`. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":468,"cache_read_input_tokens":38923,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":468},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ee44807-e628-46aa-ace4-4ea26444fb50","uuid":"98524f8c-0a11-4822-a860-682f51669518","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:17:24.052Z","request_id":"req_011CgS6XeeX2rrSJtUzgrPhf"}
